1
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:13,340
Try letting peace go
lightly and stepping away.

2
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:26,880
Aiming for a certain day
floating on the Nakagawa,

3
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:33,980
kick a pebble and even your shoes fly off.

4
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:42,220
And onto the carpenter's head,
who had been saving his money,

5
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:48,460
they laughed that he was still just a brat.

6
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:53,560
Even if I drop my energy somewhere,

7
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:57,140
Katsushika, Kameari, one more yawn.

8
00:00:57,140 --> 00:01:02,500
The unchanging streetscape
is strangely kind.

9
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:10,460
From the pointed hat's water vessel,

10
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:16,780
the great shaku heavens,
the setting sun falls.

11
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:25,260
Tomorrow too, it will end just like this.

12
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:30,400
Katsushika, Shibamata,
again, even happiness lost.

13
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:33,900
Because I'm a foolish me
who has finally realized it.

14
00:01:39,540 --> 00:01:41,220
Let's play a baseball game!

15
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:46,220
What is this?

16
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:50,460
It's a baseball board. The one I
used when I was in elementary school.

17
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:52,340
How do you play it?

18
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:54,340
What, Nakagawa, you don't know either?

19
00:01:54,880 --> 00:01:56,760
The rules are the same as baseball.

20
00:01:56,760 --> 00:02:00,900
Pull and release this pitching lever,
and the pitcher throws the ball.

21
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:01,960
Then you hit it.

22
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:04,760
If it goes into this hole, it's a hit.

23
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:07,400
Wow, it's really simple, isn't it?

24
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:09,240
This looks like something anyone could play.

25
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:14,240
How about this? Let's play a match,
and the loser buys lunch.

26
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:17,140
That sounds fun, let's do it, senpai.

27
00:02:17,140 --> 00:02:19,840
Good luck, Kei-chan.
This match is gobu gobu!

28
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:22,900
Exactly, it all comes down to luck.

29
00:02:23,460 --> 00:02:26,660
But Gitchon baseball board game has real depth,
you know.

30
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:28,860
Then let's start the match right away!

31
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:30,820
I'll go first, all right?

32
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:32,200
Sure.

33
00:02:32,660 --> 00:02:35,340
There's also a lever attached here.

34
00:02:35,340 --> 00:02:38,220
No, that's just decoration,
purely decoration.

35
00:02:38,220 --> 00:02:39,840
Come on, let's get started!

36
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:41,200
Alright then, here I go.

37
00:02:43,420 --> 00:02:44,560
Home run!

38
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:46,720
Well, looks like I'm on a roll.

39
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:47,400
Yes!

40
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:50,600
Yay, three outs, we're switching!

41
00:02:51,360 --> 00:02:53,180
Down two runs right off the bat

42
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:56,500
It's fine, it's only the first inning.
We can still come back!

43
00:02:56,500 --> 00:02:57,980
Yes, I'll do my best.

44
00:02:57,980 --> 00:03:00,680
That's right, coming back is easy, easy.

45
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:01,460
Here I go.

46
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,680
The ball curved!

47
00:03:05,680 --> 00:03:06,780
What's going on?

48
00:03:06,780 --> 00:03:10,620
Lucky, lucky. After all, it's all just luck.

49
00:03:14,300 --> 00:03:15,460
I got hit again.

50
00:03:15,460 --> 00:03:17,520
Sorry, I'm the only one
getting all the lucky breaks.

51
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:18,800
I'm home.

52
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:20,760
Thanks for your hard work.

53
00:03:21,180 --> 00:03:24,280
It's the baseball board game!
Brings back memories.

54
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:26,320
I used to play it all the time as a kid.

55
00:03:26,860 --> 00:03:27,700
Is this a curveball...?

56
00:03:27,700 --> 00:03:28,720
Hey, Terai.

57
00:03:28,720 --> 00:03:30,680
Ryo-chan, be quiet!

58
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:32,040
What do you mean?

59
00:03:32,220 --> 00:03:34,960
It's a breaking ball.
The ball's made of iron, right?

60
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:38,520
Use the lever to move the
magnet under the game board

61
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:40,360
and throw curveballs and shoots.

62
00:03:41,820 --> 00:03:42,620
Senpai.

63
00:03:42,620 --> 00:03:43,280
Ryo-chan.

64
00:03:43,280 --> 00:03:45,240
I just remembered.

65
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:48,140
Right, we could throw breaking balls too,
couldn't we?

66
00:03:48,140 --> 00:03:49,060
How convenient.

67
00:03:50,720 --> 00:03:51,900
Come on, that kind of thing.

68
00:03:51,900 --> 00:03:53,800
Then you can use curveballs too.

69
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:56,940
Damn it,
that Terai said something he shouldn't have.

70
00:03:56,940 --> 00:03:59,580
But I still have a trick up my sleeve.

71
00:04:00,220 --> 00:04:01,460
Alright, here I go.

72
00:04:04,700 --> 00:04:06,980
Try moving the magnet again.

73
00:04:06,980 --> 00:04:11,840
It's the iron filings.

74
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:14,760
This time, try moving it while
looking into Ryo-san's eyes.

75
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:18,900
He's reading our hands from
how the iron filings move.

76
00:04:20,840 --> 00:04:24,760
So that's how it is.
What should I do? Just do as I say!

77
00:04:24,760 --> 00:04:27,100
What's wrong? It's still two outs!

78
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:30,300
Yes, sorry to keep you waiting. Here I go.

79
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:32,980
That's a curveball

80
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:36,420
Damn it.

81
00:04:36,420 --> 00:04:37,060
Yes!

82
00:04:37,060 --> 00:04:37,900
Three outs, change sides!

83
00:04:38,340 --> 00:04:43,600
Ryo-san doesn't seem to realize
we've figured out his cheating.

84
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:46,360
This time, let's use it against him.

85
00:04:46,360 --> 00:04:49,080
What? I'm still way ahead!

86
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:51,400
Are you really going to keep it up?

87
00:04:51,780 --> 00:04:52,240
Here I come!

88
00:04:52,380 --> 00:04:52,740
Here!

89
00:04:53,020 --> 00:04:53,640
Victory!

90
00:04:55,940 --> 00:04:56,840
Yes!

91
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,200
Wow! It's a home run!

92
00:04:58,500 --> 00:05:00,680
Damn it! You got lucky, didn't you!

93
00:05:01,460 --> 00:05:02,920
Now it's a curveball

94
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:03,580
Take this!

95
00:05:04,280 --> 00:05:04,640
There!

96
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:06,820
Now it's third base!

97
00:05:07,540 --> 00:05:08,620
W-what? How?

98
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:12,840
Wow! She caught up in no time!

99
00:05:14,820 --> 00:05:16,800
And it's a walk-off, one-hit comeback!

100
00:05:17,340 --> 00:05:18,780
W-what's going on?

101
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:20,960
Hey,

102
00:05:21,010 --> 00:05:24,840
Terai! Everything's gone haywire since you showed up!
What did you teach Nakagawa?

103
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:27,304
I just taught him the sneaky trick

104
00:05:27,354 --> 00:05:29,800
that cheaters use, the iron-sand trick.

105
00:05:29,820 --> 00:05:33,580
What? Lunch money is on the line,
and you had to go and stick your nose in!

106
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:35,140
Ryo-chan, stop it!

107
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:39,140
It's your fault, senior, for cheating!
Come on, let's keep playing!

108
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:43,011
Damn, at this rate we'll
be overtaken and lose.

109
00:05:43,061 --> 00:05:44,360
Since it's come to this...

110
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:45,240
Terai error!

111
00:05:49,540 --> 00:05:53,300
No, no. I got carried away
and broke the baseball board.

112
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:56,260
Well, let's call it a draw and go get lunch.

113
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:58,300
I can't accept that.

114
00:05:58,600 --> 00:06:02,300
That's right. If we'd kept going,
Kei-chan would have definitely won.

115
00:06:02,500 --> 00:06:05,180
It can't be helped. It broke, after all.

116
00:06:05,460 --> 00:06:06,600
You broke it on purpose, didn't you.

117
00:06:06,640 --> 00:06:07,380
I didn't do it on purpose.

118
00:06:07,940 --> 00:06:08,740
Fine, I understand.

119
00:06:08,790 --> 00:06:13,040
Then let's settle it with
Super Real Simulation Baseball.

120
00:06:13,340 --> 00:06:17,880
That's the one where you become a pro baseball
team owner and build the best team in Japan, right?

121
00:06:19,540 --> 00:06:21,220
Let's put it on the big screen.

122
00:06:21,220 --> 00:06:22,380
Sounds fun.

123
00:06:22,380 --> 00:06:23,820
Let me join in too.

124
00:06:23,820 --> 00:06:26,540
Actually,
I've been hooked on it myself lately.

125
00:06:26,540 --> 00:06:29,060
It's the steady,
step-by-step building that makes it good.

126
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:30,540
I'm not one for that kind of...

127
00:06:30,540 --> 00:06:32,220
A game like that is more Terai's style.

128
00:06:32,220 --> 00:06:33,580
Are you running away?

129
00:06:33,580 --> 00:06:36,940
What? You've got some nerve,
calling out a game master like me.

130
00:06:37,420 --> 00:06:39,100
Fine, I'll take the field and face you.

131
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:45,120
Come on, let's start the game already

132
00:06:45,860 --> 00:06:46,920
Terai still hasn't

133
00:06:47,680 --> 00:06:50,480
Apparently he got lost in the garden

134
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:53,320
A security helicopter
is searching for him now

135
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:54,340
Honestly

136
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:57,440
Sorry, sorry, I thought that might happen

137
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:01,880
Whoa, so you're going to
project it onto this screen

138
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:04,700
Yes, it's very realistic and powerful

139
00:07:05,280 --> 00:07:07,660
No matter what game it is, you won't beat me

140
00:07:09,660 --> 00:07:11,160
So what do we do first?

141
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:15,520
With the controller, you register as owner
and choose your old team name and uniforms

142
00:07:16,920 --> 00:07:18,760
have already been scanned
and imported in advance.

143
00:07:19,500 --> 00:07:21,600
Next, we'll decide the team name.

144
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:24,160
This is pretty serious.

145
00:07:24,780 --> 00:07:28,880
For the owner registration,
the team name is -

146
00:07:28,880 --> 00:07:31,320
Ryotsu Zenia Ares!

147
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:33,060
Next, the uniforms.

148
00:07:33,060 --> 00:07:34,800
This one!

149
00:07:35,640 --> 00:07:39,380
The starting capital for running the
team is 1 billion yen each to begin with.

150
00:07:39,380 --> 00:07:43,520
Use that to recruit players,
the manager, and the coaches.

151
00:07:43,520 --> 00:07:49,960
Alright, for pitchers, let's take Higashiguchi from last year's San Burasho and Sasahara,
the Mountain Great Demon.

152
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:53,980
For catcher, Furuki,
the MVP, and Yashiro Hachiryō.

153
00:07:53,980 --> 00:07:58,720
Ryo-san, if you gather only players with high salaries,
you'll go bankrupt!

154
00:07:58,720 --> 00:08:00,160
If we go bankrupt, we lose.

155
00:08:00,160 --> 00:08:01,000
Th-that's right.

156
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:04,220
At first,
keep just one or two high-salary players.

157
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:08,260
For the rest, recruit rookies and
low-salary players and develop them.

158
00:08:08,260 --> 00:08:10,620
At first, we only need three pitchers.

159
00:08:10,620 --> 00:08:11,520
This is such a hassle.

160
00:08:13,520 --> 00:08:15,880
Once the team is complete,
the game will finally begin.

161
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:19,340
Alright, today's game is the
Nakagawa Konzerns Tournament.

162
00:08:19,340 --> 00:08:20,720
This is quite the atmosphere.

163
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:22,860
Then I'll take the first turn.

164
00:08:22,860 --> 00:08:24,000
Play ball!

165
00:08:25,520 --> 00:08:27,880
Why is Nakagawa inside the game?

166
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:32,000
If the owner registers himself as manager,
he can take part in the game.

167
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:34,000
Then you should have told me that earlier.

168
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,820
I'm going to become an owner-manager too!

169
00:08:35,820 --> 00:08:38,220
Here comes the pitch,
the pitcher winds up and throws!

170
00:08:38,220 --> 00:08:38,680
He hit it!

171
00:08:38,680 --> 00:08:41,260
A home run, and another home run!

172
00:08:41,940 --> 00:08:42,660
Again.

173
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:45,600
When does the pitcher get replaced?

174
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:46,820
Again?

175
00:08:46,820 --> 00:08:47,300
Shut up!

176
00:08:48,700 --> 00:08:49,640
What are you doing?

177
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:52,020
There's no relief pitcher to bring in.

178
00:08:52,020 --> 00:08:54,680
You said at the start we could only use three players,
didn't you?

179
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:57,000
Then the pitcher is...

180
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:59,300
The pitcher is Yamada from right field!

181
00:09:00,340 --> 00:09:02,300
You can't use players like that.

182
00:09:02,300 --> 00:09:04,120
Shut up, mind your own business!

183
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:06,160
Useless pitcher, get off already!

184
00:09:06,160 --> 00:09:08,520
What a sudden turn of events!

185
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:08,960
Seriously?

186
00:09:09,520 --> 00:09:11,000
Alright, the game resumes!

187
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:12,640
The pitcher threw, and it was hit.

188
00:09:13,540 --> 00:09:21,740
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

189
00:09:21,740 --> 00:09:24,960
After seven innings, it's 38 to 0.

190
00:09:25,540 --> 00:09:27,700
Looks like the game's decided

191
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:29,700
What should we do, senpai?

192
00:09:29,700 --> 00:09:31,720
Let's just forfeit the game.

193
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:32,780
Scratch that.

194
00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:36,600
Senpai

195
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:38,160
Ryo-chan, that's dirty!

196
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:40,400
It's my first time, so what's the harm?

197
00:09:40,400 --> 00:09:42,260
Make sure Kei-chan doesn't get beaten again.

198
00:09:42,260 --> 00:09:43,840
Freeze the reset button.

199
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:44,560
Got it.

200
00:09:44,560 --> 00:09:48,080
Ryo-chan,
making you the pitcher and the catcher too!

201
00:09:48,080 --> 00:09:49,820
Don't cheat again, okay?

202
00:09:51,740 --> 00:09:52,680
No way, senpai.

203
00:09:54,420 --> 00:09:56,700
It's annoying,
but that's a reasonable opinion.

204
00:09:57,200 --> 00:09:59,840
Ryo-san hates doing things step by step,
doesn't he.

205
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:02,200
Developing players is a hassle for him.

206
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:03,000
Got it.

207
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:06,040
I'll go along with Ryo-san
to develop the pitcher.

208
00:10:06,040 --> 00:10:08,800
Nakagawa, Reiko,
could you two keep playing the game?

209
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:09,740
Fine.

210
00:10:10,300 --> 00:10:11,540
Let's do it, Kei-chan.

211
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:16,460
Come on, Ryo-san.

212
00:10:16,460 --> 00:10:19,540
The basics are developing
the players you draft.

213
00:10:19,540 --> 00:10:20,140
Got it.

214
00:10:21,740 --> 00:10:23,060
We'll reinforce the roster
and train them thoroughly.

215
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:26,040
This ground looks rather shabby, doesn't it?

216
00:10:26,040 --> 00:10:28,160
We can't spend money on the farm team,
you know.

217
00:10:35,540 --> 00:10:37,320
Hey, stop slacking off!

218
00:10:38,080 --> 00:10:40,220
The training's too tough, I can't keep up.

219
00:10:40,820 --> 00:10:43,100
What? You dare defy the manager?

220
00:10:43,700 --> 00:10:45,140
You two are both fired.

221
00:10:45,700 --> 00:10:48,900
Ryo-san, if you do that,
we'll have no pitchers left!

222
00:10:48,900 --> 00:10:51,140
Right, reset it.

223
00:10:51,740 --> 00:10:55,200
Damn you, Nakagawa,
you had to go and mess things up!

224
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:58,540
Terai, how do we get a pitcher?

225
00:10:58,900 --> 00:11:01,260
We've got no choice but to
buy one again with money.

226
00:11:01,260 --> 00:11:02,880
How much money do we have left?

227
00:11:02,880 --> 00:11:04,340
We only have 5 million.

228
00:11:04,340 --> 00:11:06,060
At this rate, we'll never

229
00:11:06,060 --> 00:11:08,260
No, there must be some kind of trick.

230
00:11:08,260 --> 00:11:11,240
The owner can take a side job!

231
00:11:12,060 --> 00:11:13,220
Horse racing!

232
00:11:13,820 --> 00:11:16,560
They've even got a method that suits me

233
00:11:17,040 --> 00:11:19,620
But there's also a chance
we could go bankrupt.

234
00:11:19,620 --> 00:11:21,240
Who do you think I am?

235
00:11:21,740 --> 00:11:24,820
I'll turn 5 million into 100 times,
no, 1000 times!

236
00:11:25,880 --> 00:11:28,996
Alright, the top of the ninth is over,
and the score is 3 to 2,

237
00:11:29,046 --> 00:11:31,380
with the Akimoto Beauties in the lead!

238
00:11:33,080 --> 00:11:35,640
But the Nakagawa Konzerns,
in the bottom of the ninth,

239
00:11:35,690 --> 00:11:37,840
with two outs, have a runner on second!

240
00:11:38,460 --> 00:11:42,000
Alright, a hit ties it!
A home run and it's a walk-off win!

241
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:44,320
Not so fast! Kei-chan, here's the showdown!

242
00:11:44,900 --> 00:11:46,760
The pitcher throws, and he swings!

243
00:11:47,220 --> 00:11:48,180
It's going! It's going!

244
00:11:48,620 --> 00:11:50,340
Yes! Keep going! Go, go!

245
00:11:51,760 --> 00:11:53,500
A walk-off home run!

246
00:11:53,500 --> 00:11:54,360
Yay!

247
00:11:55,680 --> 00:11:57,400
Ryo-chan, that's just cruel.

248
00:11:57,400 --> 00:11:59,900
Think about how I feel,
losing on a walk-off like that.

249
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:01,480
Don't get the wrong idea.

250
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:04,460
I hit a huge horse racing payout
and grabbed 100 billion yen.

251
00:12:05,340 --> 00:12:06,600
100 billion yen?

252
00:12:08,720 --> 00:12:12,460
Now we can buy good pitchers
from the majors by the truckload!

253
00:12:24,780 --> 00:12:25,560
Aaaaaah!

254
00:12:27,400 --> 00:12:38,060
With 100 billion yen, this is just the start!
Look, they all look strong! Take your pick! I want you to play in Japan!

255
00:12:38,060 --> 00:12:43,600
I'd consider it if the signing bonus were 1 billion yen!
That's way too high! Who do you think you are?

256
00:12:44,800 --> 00:12:51,680
Japanese players are practically giving themselves away What a negotiation...
it's almost like blackmail.

257
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:55,220
I haggled them down good!

258
00:12:55,220 --> 00:12:59,640
Look! A legion of invincible ones,
ten pitchers and batters!

259
00:12:59,640 --> 00:13:03,640
Even if you bring that many,
a team can only have three foreign players.

260
00:13:03,640 --> 00:13:06,100
What, that rule? I'll change it myself.

261
00:13:06,980 --> 00:13:10,840
I'll spend as much money as I need!
I'm becoming commissioner, so you retire!

262
00:13:10,840 --> 00:13:11,520
No way.

263
00:13:11,880 --> 00:13:13,180
Ugh, take this, then!

264
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:15,020
Absolutely not!

265
00:13:15,380 --> 00:13:19,180
Obviously! A commissioner doesn't change just because of that,
you know.

266
00:13:19,180 --> 00:13:21,240
Yeah, then we're going
all-out attack for sure!

267
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:24,000
Alright! Go, go! Full speed ahead! Come on!

268
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:26,180
Yahahahaha!

269
00:13:26,260 --> 00:13:28,100
Maybe I'll switch out the commissioner.

270
00:13:28,680 --> 00:13:32,100
Yes! Now the three foreign
player slots are abolished!

271
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:34,600
You really pulled off an outrageous loophole,
didn't you.

272
00:13:34,840 --> 00:13:35,860
It's Ryo-chan, after all.

273
00:13:36,260 --> 00:13:38,800
Alright! Ryo and the Zenia Lies
are finally taking the field!

274
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:39,920
Who's the opponent?

275
00:13:40,640 --> 00:13:42,300
It's a three-game series against Terai.

276
00:13:42,840 --> 00:13:44,260
Somehow, that's scary.

277
00:13:47,300 --> 00:13:48,160
Play ball!

278
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:50,800
Alright! We're going on the attack!

279
00:13:51,680 --> 00:13:53,060
And now,
the much-anticipated ninth inning...

280
00:13:53,060 --> 00:13:55,180
It's gone! A home run right off the bat!

281
00:13:55,240 --> 00:13:56,020
Yeah!

282
00:13:56,020 --> 00:13:58,760
See that, you guys?
Talent is something you buy with money!

283
00:13:58,760 --> 00:14:00,200
Money makes the world go round!

284
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:09,140
What are you doing, slowpoke?
Hurry up and pitch!

285
00:14:09,140 --> 00:14:12,100
Hold on, I'm taking notes
on the foreign players' data.

286
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:15,400
Pulling petty little stunts like that,
you're as useless as earwax.

287
00:14:16,340 --> 00:14:21,060
It's pointless. By the time the data's gathered,
I'll have swapped in new foreigners one after another.

288
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:22,420
No way...

289
00:14:22,420 --> 00:14:22,768
Well,

290
00:14:22,818 --> 00:14:27,340
your motto is to live steadily
with sacrifice bunts, right?

291
00:14:27,340 --> 00:14:28,160
No wonder.

292
00:14:28,160 --> 00:14:30,460
Go on living that way,
for the rest of your life.

293
00:14:31,760 --> 00:14:34,620
Me, on the other hand,
I live by the home run philosophy.

294
00:14:34,620 --> 00:14:37,600
I don't resort to cheap tricks
like bunts or squeeze plays.

295
00:14:39,280 --> 00:14:41,160
The only sign I give is for the home run.

296
00:14:43,380 --> 00:14:45,020
Alright, game set!

297
00:14:45,020 --> 00:14:47,980
An easy win, 79 to 0!

298
00:14:50,840 --> 00:14:52,640
Are you even motivated
for the next two games?

299
00:14:53,020 --> 00:14:54,800
I think it's a waste of time, though.

300
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:56,520
We'll play them anyway.

301
00:14:57,060 --> 00:15:02,120
The starter, Nolan Liner, looks pretty worn out,
just like in the first game.

302
00:15:02,520 --> 00:15:04,380
Are we using the same pitcher again?

303
00:15:04,660 --> 00:15:05,340
Yep.

304
00:15:05,340 --> 00:15:07,480
At least give him a few days off.

305
00:15:07,480 --> 00:15:10,160
This guy cost us 500 million yen.

306
00:15:10,160 --> 00:15:12,540
Wouldn't it be a waste
to rest him even one day?

307
00:15:13,240 --> 00:15:16,020
Some players burn out from pitching back-to-back games,
you know.

308
00:15:17,980 --> 00:15:19,220
You can't have everything, Ryo-chan.

309
00:15:19,620 --> 00:15:20,600
Play ball!

310
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:22,400
Alright, here we go!

311
00:15:22,940 --> 00:15:24,660
And now, the first pitch to watch.

312
00:15:25,140 --> 00:15:25,820
Catch it!

313
00:15:26,380 --> 00:15:27,920
Aw, he got hit!

314
00:15:28,370 --> 00:15:28,820
Yes!

315
00:15:28,820 --> 00:15:29,780
That bastard!

316
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:31,800
What the hell are you doing, you idiot?

317
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:35,660
My shoulder hurts, I can't pitch.

318
00:15:35,660 --> 00:15:36,920
Please let me rest.

319
00:15:37,540 --> 00:15:37,880
What?

320
00:15:38,380 --> 00:15:39,400
Don't go slacking off!

321
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:41,380
Throw until your arm breaks!

322
00:15:41,380 --> 00:15:42,980
He stays in. He stays in the game.

323
00:15:44,220 --> 00:15:46,160
Runner on first. The pitcher's thrown.

324
00:15:48,400 --> 00:15:49,380
That bastard

325
00:15:49,780 --> 00:15:50,760
You're fired!

326
00:15:50,760 --> 00:15:52,760
There are plenty of backup pitchers.

327
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:53,980
Gonzalez, then.

328
00:15:53,980 --> 00:15:56,700
Gonzalez went back home for
something to do with his wife.

329
00:15:57,040 --> 00:15:58,720
What? Then Tomason.

330
00:15:58,720 --> 00:16:00,920
Tomason also suddenly has some errand,
apparently.

331
00:16:00,920 --> 00:16:01,600
What did you say?

332
00:16:01,600 --> 00:16:03,540
I told you so.

333
00:16:03,540 --> 00:16:05,300
Because you used him so badly.

334
00:16:05,300 --> 00:16:06,840
Mind your own business!

335
00:16:06,840 --> 00:16:09,220
Teraijimi Cheese takes a four-run lead.

336
00:16:09,220 --> 00:16:10,520
Still one out, bases loaded.

337
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:11,420
The pitcher throws!

338
00:16:11,420 --> 00:16:12,500
It's a quiz!

339
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:14,860
Yay!

340
00:16:15,340 --> 00:16:15,840
Nice!

341
00:16:15,840 --> 00:16:16,960
One more run!

342
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:19,760
Don't really score runs by bunting!

343
00:16:19,760 --> 00:16:22,220
That's a lifelong sacrifice bunt, isn't it?

344
00:16:22,220 --> 00:16:23,000
But...

345
00:16:23,620 --> 00:16:26,140
Okay, three outs!
We're getting those points back!

346
00:16:29,700 --> 00:16:30,840
It's the home run sign!

347
00:16:30,840 --> 00:16:31,520
Go, go!

348
00:16:32,860 --> 00:16:34,500
They're really calling it out!

349
00:16:35,480 --> 00:16:36,160
Slide!

350
00:16:36,160 --> 00:16:37,000
Out again.

351
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:39,780
Damn, these foreign players are in a slump.

352
00:16:40,380 --> 00:16:41,560
That's not it, senpai.

353
00:16:42,180 --> 00:16:45,000
Terai-san has been pulling up the foreign players' data
on and off this whole time.

354
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:45,960
That's why.

355
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:47,900
They're reading the
courses you're weak against.

356
00:16:47,900 --> 00:16:48,260
What?

357
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:49,820
Terai-sama.

358
00:16:49,820 --> 00:16:53,680
Well, I can't spend money
like Ryo-san does, either.

359
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:55,460
We have to win with strategy.

360
00:16:55,460 --> 00:16:59,680
We're making the most of our limited
strength with teamwork and strategy.

361
00:16:59,680 --> 00:17:03,000
Yes, of course they're strong when
you spend billions of yen on them.

362
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:06,980
Terai-san carefully manages and develops each player,
one by one.

363
00:17:06,980 --> 00:17:08,600
And the senior bench player...

364
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:12,060
Don't you dare hold back!

365
00:17:12,060 --> 00:17:17,140
I'm a designated hitter by nature.
I'm bad at defense.

366
00:17:17,140 --> 00:17:21,360
Shut up! There are plenty of replacements.
You're fired!

367
00:17:23,360 --> 00:17:25,220
Hey, hurry up and throw!

368
00:17:25,220 --> 00:17:29,260
If he throws any more, his shoulder will break.
Please, I'm begging you.

369
00:17:29,820 --> 00:17:34,260
Idiot! I've spent 300 million on you, so you'll
keep pitching until I get my money's worth.

370
00:17:34,780 --> 00:17:41,640
Senpai only ever goes on the attack and doesn't consider players' aptitude.
You'll ruin even good pitchers by making them pitch back-to-back.

371
00:17:42,260 --> 00:17:45,840
Your strategies are so sloppy.
They're all about whatever works right now.

372
00:17:46,800 --> 00:17:50,580
That's right. And when the players are ruined,
you'll just buy more with money, won't you?

373
00:17:50,580 --> 00:17:51,420
Shut up!

374
00:17:52,100 --> 00:17:56,280
Mind your own business! If you think opinions like that will make me reflect,
you're dead wrong!

375
00:17:56,360 --> 00:17:59,920
When someone tells me no, I hit back with 100 times the force.
That's my principle!

376
00:18:00,060 --> 00:18:01,860
I'm going to keep throwing money around!

377
00:18:03,140 --> 00:18:06,140
First, we'll trade money for
one of Nakagawa's team's players.

378
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:08,680
I'll poach their ace!

379
00:18:08,680 --> 00:18:10,480
I don't think that's going to work.

380
00:18:12,060 --> 00:18:12,420
Come on over.

381
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:13,840
No, thanks.

382
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:15,160
See?

383
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:17,460
Is that so? How about this?

384
00:18:18,380 --> 00:18:20,420
You've been waiting for this, haven't you?
It's one billion yen!

385
00:18:21,480 --> 00:18:24,860
I'll sign the contract!

386
00:18:24,860 --> 00:18:25,440
Hah...

387
00:18:25,440 --> 00:18:28,679
See? In this world, slap the other
guy's cheeks with stacks of cash

388
00:18:28,729 --> 00:18:31,160
two or three times,
and they'll all do whatever I say.

389
00:18:31,800 --> 00:18:34,160
Good. Reiko's key players are mine, too.

390
00:18:34,160 --> 00:18:37,060
Sorry, but these players
don't move for money.

391
00:18:37,780 --> 00:18:39,600
Then I have another option.

392
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:43,940
I'll pay double Reiko's salary, and get
them lots of commercial appearances too!

393
00:18:44,300 --> 00:18:45,200
That's not all.

394
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:48,680
And you can even date a
gorgeous female announcer!

395
00:18:48,680 --> 00:18:50,820
I'll sign the contract.

396
00:18:51,900 --> 00:18:52,620
N-no way

397
00:18:52,620 --> 00:18:56,220
We've thoroughly looked
into the players' habits.

398
00:18:56,220 --> 00:18:58,940
yet you won't bother
gathering baseball data!

399
00:18:58,940 --> 00:19:00,260
This is just the beginning.

400
00:19:00,260 --> 00:19:03,660
We'll bring back top players from the majors,
no expense spared.

401
00:19:05,040 --> 00:19:07,000
It's a renovation that cost 10 billion yen.

402
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:09,200
We've got twenty pitchers alone, after all.

403
00:19:10,580 --> 00:19:13,180
I'll make quick work of
them with 160 km/h fastballs.

404
00:19:16,020 --> 00:19:17,180
Why are we getting hit?

405
00:19:17,180 --> 00:19:19,540
That pitch was right in
the batter's wheelhouse.

406
00:19:19,540 --> 00:19:20,820
That's a home run for sure.

407
00:19:21,260 --> 00:19:22,280
We'll see about that.

408
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:31,560
N-no way!

409
00:19:32,080 --> 00:19:34,760
Just in case something like this happened,
I poured fifty billion yen

410
00:19:34,760 --> 00:19:37,360
into remodeling the
stadium with movable stands.

411
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:39,600
Cheating, Ryo-san!

412
00:19:39,600 --> 00:19:41,120
Protesting to the umpires,

413
00:19:41,700 --> 00:19:43,180
that was against the rules!

414
00:19:43,180 --> 00:19:44,320
Please do it over.

415
00:19:44,320 --> 00:19:45,440
No can do.

416
00:19:45,440 --> 00:19:46,140
Because

417
00:19:46,760 --> 00:19:48,580
I'm the head umpire, after all.

418
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:51,500
It's not just the head umpire!

419
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:55,180
The base umpires are all me, too!

420
00:19:57,100 --> 00:19:58,680
Wh-when did that happen?

421
00:19:59,820 --> 00:20:03,300
Fire all the umpires and
register me as one of them.

422
00:20:03,300 --> 00:20:04,340
Ryo-chan.

423
00:20:04,760 --> 00:20:07,480
This is the money!
No matter what tricks I use, I'll win!

424
00:20:08,340 --> 00:20:10,200
Alright, we'll just call it a loss, Ryo-san.

425
00:20:10,660 --> 00:20:13,620
Right. Let's call it Ryo-chan's
championship and end it there.

426
00:20:14,020 --> 00:20:15,780
Then it's my championship,
so that's settled.

427
00:20:16,320 --> 00:20:16,700
Wait, please!

428
00:20:17,580 --> 00:20:20,320
I just made 200 billion
yen in stock trading!

429
00:20:21,100 --> 00:20:21,420
What?

430
00:20:22,320 --> 00:20:25,080
With this,
I'll topple Commissioner Zakara, Senior!

431
00:20:25,420 --> 00:20:27,420
Like I'd let you topple me that easily!

432
00:20:27,960 --> 00:20:30,017
Nyaha! Money, money! Nakagawa-kun,

433
00:20:30,067 --> 00:20:33,300
from today, you're the commissioner!
Nyahahaha!

434
00:20:39,140 --> 00:20:40,120
You're weak when it comes to money,
aren't you?

435
00:20:40,820 --> 00:20:42,380
With this, I'm the commissioner.

436
00:20:42,380 --> 00:20:44,820
Stadiums with movable stands are abolished.

437
00:20:44,820 --> 00:20:47,780
And all the senior
umpires will be fired too.

438
00:20:47,780 --> 00:20:48,740
W-what?

439
00:20:52,820 --> 00:20:54,960
M-me too? I've been fired!

440
00:20:55,840 --> 00:20:57,760
Good, now we can fight on equal terms.

441
00:20:57,760 --> 00:20:59,380
Ryo-san, let's continue the game.

442
00:20:59,380 --> 00:21:00,420
Wait, please.

443
00:21:00,420 --> 00:21:02,460
We still have 50 billion yen left.

444
00:21:02,460 --> 00:21:05,480
I'll bring Suketto over
to Terai's team for you.

445
00:21:10,860 --> 00:21:16,680
Whoa, aren't these the Brains players
who won the World Series last year?

446
00:21:17,140 --> 00:21:21,340
Come on, Terai-san,
now beat that senior who uses dirty tricks.

447
00:21:21,340 --> 00:21:24,520
We have the data,
and with this lineup we're sure to win.

448
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:28,880
Uh-oh, if we resume the game like this,
we'll lose.

449
00:21:29,260 --> 00:21:30,940
Isn't there some way to win?

450
00:21:31,600 --> 00:21:32,400
Ryo-san.

451
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:34,280
Hold on, time out!

452
00:21:34,880 --> 00:21:37,400
Every game has an ultimate trick.

453
00:21:39,220 --> 00:21:40,420
We need to find it.

454
00:21:42,020 --> 00:21:42,460
This...

455
00:21:44,080 --> 00:21:46,040
Bad timing, you know.

456
00:21:46,040 --> 00:21:46,500
Ryo-chan.

457
00:21:46,500 --> 00:21:48,620
Nothing you do is going to work anymore.

458
00:21:48,620 --> 00:21:50,180
Shut up and be quiet for a while.

459
00:21:50,180 --> 00:21:50,900
This is...

460
00:21:54,100 --> 00:21:55,580
All the players...

461
00:21:55,580 --> 00:21:56,240
are being substituted!

462
00:22:00,820 --> 00:22:01,700
Wait, what is this?

463
00:22:04,840 --> 00:22:06,400
They're all Ryo-chan's guys!

464
00:22:08,400 --> 00:22:16,800
There's no rule saying the owner can't play, right?
Alright, game on, playboy.

465
00:22:23,920 --> 00:22:27,040
Oh no, my eyes are burning,
I've got a bad feeling about this.

466
00:22:32,260 --> 00:22:33,460
Now!

467
00:22:39,040 --> 00:22:42,480
Hahahaha! How about that!
This is the phantom magic ball,

468
00:22:42,530 --> 00:22:43,500
the Magic Armor Ball!

469
00:22:43,900 --> 00:22:45,340
You hit him on purpose!

470
00:22:45,520 --> 00:22:46,100
That's dirty!

471
00:22:46,480 --> 00:22:47,700
That's low, Ryo-san!

472
00:22:50,680 --> 00:22:51,840
I've been waiting for this.

473
00:22:51,840 --> 00:22:52,880
Everyone, go!

474
00:22:55,180 --> 00:22:56,140
It's a brawl!

475
00:22:56,140 --> 00:22:56,640
No way.

476
00:23:07,080 --> 00:23:09,200
Even the spectators are all Ryo-chan.

477
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:10,920
What kind of trick is this, anyway?

478
00:23:10,920 --> 00:23:12,800
We're going to Mars too!

479
00:23:13,620 --> 00:23:14,980
Go, go, go!

480
00:23:15,980 --> 00:23:16,840
We did it!

481
00:23:17,140 --> 00:23:18,980
We did it!

482
00:23:22,380 --> 00:23:24,440
This is the ultimate trick!

483
00:23:24,900 --> 00:23:25,940
This is absurd!

484
00:23:27,160 --> 00:23:29,720
The company's ridiculously good at fighting!

485
00:23:29,860 --> 00:23:31,260
We're going home too!

486
00:23:31,860 --> 00:23:33,880
By forfeit, we win!

487
00:23:34,240 --> 00:23:38,280
Idiot! Idiot! Idiot!

488
00:23:38,280 --> 00:23:41,520
Trying to beat me?
You've got a hundred years to go!

489
00:23:41,680 --> 00:23:43,580
Now, the next opponent is...

490
00:23:43,580 --> 00:24:03,400
Everyone, what's going on?!
!

491
00:24:06,200 --> 00:24:07,920
Komachi and me getting married?

492
00:24:08,720 --> 00:24:10,100
N-no, you've got it wrong!

493
00:24:10,100 --> 00:24:11,440
Dad, Mom...

494
00:24:11,440 --> 00:24:14,040
No, this "Dad, Mom" business...

495
00:24:14,040 --> 00:24:15,860
That's not what I meant.

496
00:24:16,900 --> 00:24:19,380
Next time: "This is the one I love."

497
00:24:19,380 --> 00:24:21,300
I told you, it's not like that!

498
00:24:35,680 --> 00:24:43,900
Surprise and commotion, with spirit
and resolution, swift and settled.

499
00:24:43,900 --> 00:24:55,680
Decided, inspired, bouncing,
gathered, in action, and soaring away.

500
00:24:56,720 --> 00:25:00,340
Above all, an amazing power.

501
00:25:00,600 --> 00:25:06,400
Everyone gather, if you come here.

502
00:25:07,260 --> 00:25:12,720
Like a dream, the final energy.

503
00:25:13,680 --> 00:25:17,100
Gaze at tomorrow, believe in yesterday.

504
00:25:17,100 --> 00:25:20,000
Paint the universe, and stand on the ground.

505
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:23,720
The star of Kameari is coming,
the star of Kameari is coming!

506
00:25:26,160 --> 00:25:27,440
This should be good enough, right?

507
00:25:27,440 --> 00:25:28,920
Like hell it is!

